In our current workflow, we do a full site build and deployment every 3 weeks. If one team finishes a component early, they still have to wait for that big release.

That also means if something breaks, it affects the entire release — there’s no easy way to isolate changes, test gradually, or roll back quickly.

So I built a lightweight feature flag system using React Context and localStorage, entirely on the frontend.

It supports simple on/off toggles, percentage rollouts, user segment targeting, and it keeps flag state persistent across page refreshes.

This allows us to ship both MVP and Final versions of a component in the same bundle, and decide which one is shown dynamically — no need to rebuild or redeploy.

